{
  "x-call": "wingtip_airspace::surface_hours::call",
  "description": "When a part-time surface area is in effect, day by day from the field's today for a week, read from NASR's CLS_ARSP AIRSPACE_HRS, the Chart Supplement's AIRSPACE line (\"CLASS D SVC 0600-2200 MON-FRI, 0700-2200 SAT-SUN; OTHER TIMES CLASS E\"): the class at other times the one the line names (AIM 3-2-5a1; 14 CFR 71.61, 71.71(b)), never a guess. A time with no Z is the field's local time; Z is UTC at the offset now; Z++ is the Chart Supplement's double dagger, one hour earlier in daylight saving time, so the figure at the field's standard offset all year. Reads CONTINUOUS, time ranges, days (MON-FRI, SAT & SUN, WKEND) and seasons (16 MAR-31 OCT, OCT-MAR); anything else (holidays, BY NOTAM, SR-SS) leaves the hours not known (`known` false). Spans are local minutes from midnight, [from, to), a span past midnight carried into the next day. `in_force` and `change` are now's: in effect until `change.at`, or not until `change.at`, `next_day` where that is tomorrow; null where today's hours are not known. The engine has no clock: the host gives the field's local date, minute, UTC offset and whether in daylight saving time.",
